<section class="intro section" id="about"><div class="section-kicker"><span>01 / THE ARTIST</span><span>DETROIT ROOTS. DALLAS PRACTICE.</span></div><div class="intro-grid"><h2>A life<br>in <em>motion.</em></h2><div><p class="lead">Nycole Ray is a choreographer, dancer, and educator based in Dallas, Texas.</p><p>A Detroit native with a BFA in Dance from The California Institute of the Arts, she brings a career in performance, choreography, and artistic leadership to her work. She danced with Dallas Black Dance Theatre and Bruce Wood Dance Dallas, and she serves on the board of the International Association of Blacks in Dance.</p><a class="line-link" href="/about/">Read full biography <span>↗</span></a></div></div><div class="credentials"><div><strong>2010–2025</strong><span>Artistic Director, DBDT: Encore!</span></div><div><strong>Dunham Technique</strong><span>Certified instructor</span></div><div><strong>Board Member</strong><span>International Association of Blacks in Dance</span></div></div></section>
<section class="work section" id="work"><div class="section-kicker"><span>02 / SELECTED CHOREOGRAPHY</span><a href="/work/">FULL REPERTORY ↗</a></div><h2>Work that<br><em>moves.</em></h2><div class="works"><details open><summary><span class="number">01</span><h3>International Woman</h3><span class="year">2025</span><span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="work-detail"><p>Texas Ballet Theater</p><p>Music by Henryk Górecki<br>Premiere: Bass Performance Hall<br>Fort Worth, Texas · 2025</p></div></details><details><summary><span class="number">02</span><h3>Diaspora</h3><span class="year">2022</span><span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="work-detail"><p>Dallas Black Dance Theatre</p><p>Premiere: New Texas Symphony Orchestra at Moody Performance Hall<br>Dallas, Texas · 2022</p></div></details><details><summary><span class="number">03</span><h3>Nineteenth</h3><span class="year">2021</span><span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="work-detail"><p>Created for the centennial of the 19th Amendment.</p><p>Virtual premiere · 2021</p></div></details><details><summary><span class="number">04</span><h3>Reminisce</h3><span class="year">2020</span><span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="work-detail"><p>Dallas Black Dance Theatre</p><p>Music: John Legend and various artists<br>Premiere: Eisemann Center, Richardson, Texas · 2020</p></div></details></div><p class="other-works">Also in the repertory: Rising, Love Songs, The Breath Within, Opaque, Above &amp; Below, Samson and Delilah, and Frida, Frida and Frida.</p></section>
<section class="practice"><div class="practice-art"><img src="/assets/nycole-purple-gele-lip-refinement.webp" srcset="/assets/nycole-purple-gele-lip-refinement-556w.webp 556w, /assets/nycole-purple-gele-lip-refinement.webp 1111w" sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 50vw" width="1111" height="1416" alt="Nycole Ray wearing a purple gele and ivory floral couture, a House of Ray concept portrait" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="eyebrow">HOUSE OF RAY / NYCOLE RAY</span></div><div class="practice-copy"><p class="eyebrow">03 / EDUCATION &amp; COLLABORATION</p><h2>The next<br><em>generation.</em></h2><p>From 2010 to 2025, Nycole led DBDT: Encore!, Dallas Black Dance Theatre’s second company, mentoring emerging professional dancers. She is a certified Dunham Technique Instructor and a board member of the International Association of Blacks in Dance.</p><ul><li>Choreography commissions <span>01</span></li><li>Guest artist residencies <span>02</span></li><li>Master classes <span>03</span></li><li>Speaking engagements <span>04</span></li></ul><a class="line-link" href="/contact/">Work with Nycole <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
